<item><title>Burundi league sees upsets as Vital&apos;O FC falls</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/burundi-league-sees-upsets-as-vital-o-fc-falls-6222e9/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/burundi-league-sees-upsets-as-vital-o-fc-falls-6222e9/</guid><category>Burundi</category><description>Vision FC, Never Give Up, Rukinzo, Inter Stars, Panthère Noire, and Musongati FC secured victories in a weekend of football action.</description><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 06:23:30 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bi.jpg" length="31311" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bi.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Burundi reforms Obuha to decentralize construction projects</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/burundi-reforms-obuha-to-decentralize-construction-projects-128708/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/burundi-reforms-obuha-to-decentralize-construction-projects-128708/</guid><category>Burundi</category><description>A new decree will shift construction execution to communes and establish a director-general role, aiming to reduce currency pressure and improve project oversight.</description><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 05:38:23 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bi.jpg" length="31311" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bi.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Imbonerakure truck crash in Kabanga leaves 31 dead, sources say 75</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/imbonerakure-truck-crash-in-kabanga-leaves-31-dead-sources-6e03a0/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/imbonerakure-truck-crash-in-kabanga-leaves-31-dead-sources-6e03a0/</guid><category>Burundi</category><description>President Évariste Ndayishimiye put the death toll at 31, while anonymous security sources and local ruling-party officials say at least 75 people were killed.</description><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 19:40:26 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/imbonerakure-truck-crash-in-kabanga-leaves-31-dead-sources-6e03a0/share.jpg" length="42933" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/imbonerakure-truck-crash-in-kabanga-leaves-31-dead-sources-6e03a0/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Burundi holds senior RTNB cameraman at intelligence service after fire</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/burundi-holds-senior-rtnb-cameraman-at-intelligence-service-eac4b7/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/burundi-holds-senior-rtnb-cameraman-at-intelligence-service-eac4b7/</guid><category>Burundi</category><description>Bonaventure Niyongabo, a 60-year-old cameraman known as Gihuha, has been held since November 6 at the SNR in Bujumbura over a fire at the public broadcaster.</description><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:28:56 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bi.jpg" length="31311" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bi.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Burundi removes police general Ndababishije before his trial</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/burundi-removes-police-general-ndababishije-before-his-trial-302823/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/burundi-removes-police-general-ndababishije-before-his-trial-302823/</guid><category>Burundi</category><description>President Évariste Ndayishimiye signed a decree on November 14 dismissing Romuald Ndababishije for corruption and passport breaches, while he is detained in Bujumbura.</description><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:26:12 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bi.jpg" length="31311" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bi.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
